01:37:45.360 --> 01:37:46.070
Program.

01:37:46.070 --> 01:37:50.220
But some of the high level stats
of where Teach to Learn is.

01:37:50.220 --> 01:37:52.540
We've been around for
about four years now.

01:37:52.540 --> 01:37:55.350
And in that time, we've
had over 250 participants

01:37:55.350 --> 01:37:57.390
in 20 countries
around the world.

01:37:57.390 --> 01:37:59.520
And altogether,
they've connected

01:37:59.520 --> 01:38:02.970
for more than 1,000 hours,
which is pretty amazing when

01:38:02.970 --> 01:38:07.470
you think about where we
started from four years back.

01:38:07.470 --> 01:38:11.530
Our programs started out of
really just a single one.

01:38:11.530 --> 01:38:13.690
This mentorship program.

01:38:13.690 --> 01:38:15.900
And you can think of our
programs in two buckets.

01:38:15.900 --> 01:38:18.960
One-to-one, and one-to-many.

01:38:18.960 --> 01:38:21.150
So when Teach to
Learn just started,

01:38:21.150 --> 01:38:26.100
when our co-founders Derek
and Bob started making

01:38:26.100 --> 01:38:28.620
matches of people playing
similar instruments

01:38:28.620 --> 01:38:31.900
with similar musical
interests between musicians

01:38:31.900 --> 01:38:34.150
all around the world, that
was our mentorship program.

01:38:34.150 --> 01:38:36.810
That was a chance for--

01:38:36.810 --> 01:38:38.610
especially students
in areas where

01:38:38.610 --> 01:38:42.000
there wasn't access to
great musical resources

01:38:42.000 --> 01:38:45.270
to connect with musicians all
around the world for lessons

01:38:45.270 --> 01:38:48.720
and also out of that
cultural exchange and a lot

01:38:48.720 --> 01:38:51.570
of interesting things that
came from those conversations.

01:38:51.570 --> 01:38:54.990
And the demand for that was
really impressively high,

01:38:54.990 --> 01:38:57.013
more than we anticipated.

01:38:57.013 --> 01:38:58.680
And that's sort of
where we were when we

01:38:58.680 --> 01:39:01.440
came into the 15K Competition.

01:39:01.440 --> 01:39:04.800
That Mentorship Program had been
around for a couple of years,

01:39:04.800 --> 01:39:06.300
and we were thinking
about how do we

01:39:06.300 --> 01:39:09.240
take this to the next level.

01:39:09.240 --> 01:39:12.420
And how do we grow this out,
what programs do we add.

01:39:12.420 --> 01:39:16.800
And from that-- so we developed
another one-to-one program

01:39:16.800 --> 01:39:18.690
called The Fellowship.

01:39:18.690 --> 01:39:21.660
And the core of that is
really the peer exchange

01:39:21.660 --> 01:39:26.310
with structured conversations
over the course of 10 months,

01:39:26.310 --> 01:39:31.500
and funding for the Fellows
to create and execute

01:39:31.500 --> 01:39:34.320
on collaborative
community projects,

01:39:34.320 --> 01:39:37.410
whether that's around
music or something

01:39:37.410 --> 01:39:39.990
in their community
related to the Arts.

01:39:39.990 --> 01:39:42.780
So we were really excited to
launch the fellowship last year

01:39:42.780 --> 01:39:45.000
and that was something
we'd been starting

01:39:45.000 --> 01:39:48.390
to plan for and figure out
as we were going into the 15K

01:39:48.390 --> 01:39:50.050
last year.

01:39:50.050 --> 01:39:52.840
And in addition to those
one-to-one programs,

01:39:52.840 --> 01:39:54.990
we also have two
one-to-many programs.

01:39:54.990 --> 01:39:59.430
So the Classroom
Connect is a collection

01:39:59.430 --> 01:40:04.680
of curated virtual music and
cultural exchange modules

01:40:04.680 --> 01:40:08.010
that are offered in high
schools around the US,

01:40:08.010 --> 01:40:10.470
and Global Music Seminars
are online courses

01:40:10.470 --> 01:40:14.190
taught by musical faculty
from different places

01:40:14.190 --> 01:40:17.280
around the world
at conservatories

01:40:17.280 --> 01:40:19.650
in different countries
around the world.

01:40:19.650 --> 01:40:22.978
So those are our
four main programs

01:40:22.978 --> 01:40:24.020
just to give you a sense.

01:40:24.020 --> 01:40:25.400
I mentioned a few
of these things

01:40:25.400 --> 01:40:27.360
of where we've come from.

01:40:27.360 --> 01:40:30.250
We launched the Mentorship
Program back in 2016.

01:40:30.250 --> 01:40:34.550
In 2018, we joined
the MIT Sandbox,

01:40:34.550 --> 01:40:38.600
which was a great starting
point for us in that journey

01:40:38.600 --> 01:40:40.580
that I mentioned,
about rethinking

01:40:40.580 --> 01:40:43.760
some of what Teach
to Learn would offer

01:40:43.760 --> 01:40:45.800
and what we would
be in the future.

01:40:45.800 --> 01:40:49.530
We had our first paid
customer in January 2019,

01:40:49.530 --> 01:40:52.130
which was perfect
timing to enter

01:40:52.130 --> 01:40:54.950
into this sort of
pre-competition mentorship

01:40:54.950 --> 01:40:56.990
phase.

01:40:56.990 --> 01:40:58.910
And we actually
got a lot of value

01:40:58.910 --> 01:41:04.040
out of speaking with our mentor
during the 15K Competition,

01:41:04.040 --> 01:41:07.440
thinking about how do we really
capitalize on that first paid

01:41:07.440 --> 01:41:10.190
customer and think
about doubling down

01:41:10.190 --> 01:41:13.430
on that part of our programming.

01:41:13.430 --> 01:41:16.520
In April, we did we were
very, very excited to win

01:41:16.520 --> 01:41:19.490
the Creative Arts Competition,
and it was also an exciting

01:41:19.490 --> 01:41:22.590
month when we officially
received our 501(c)3

01:41:22.590 --> 01:41:24.670
registration.

01:41:24.670 --> 01:41:26.950
And then in October,
we launched two

01:41:26.950 --> 01:41:29.980
of the new programs, the
Fellowship and the Global Music

01:41:29.980 --> 01:41:31.450
Seminars.

01:41:31.450 --> 01:41:34.930
And now, in spring
of 2020, we've

01:41:34.930 --> 01:41:36.730
expanded the Classroom
Connect program

01:41:36.730 --> 01:41:39.910
to three high schools
in the Boston area,

01:41:39.910 --> 01:41:44.140
and we are really excited for
the Fellowship projects, too.

01:41:44.140 --> 01:41:47.680
They're just starting to wrap
up their 10 months in the coming

01:41:47.680 --> 01:41:51.040
months and the Fellows are
starting to implement and work

01:41:51.040 --> 01:41:52.730
on their community projects.

01:41:52.730 --> 01:41:56.020
We're actually working
right now to get funding

01:41:56.020 --> 01:41:59.410
to one of our Fellows who's
ready to go in Argentina.

01:41:59.410 --> 01:42:04.660
He's working on a really
interesting children's book,

01:42:04.660 --> 01:42:06.418
mapped to music.

01:42:06.418 --> 01:42:07.460
It should be really cool.

01:42:07.460 --> 01:42:09.580
So that's just
starting to happen,

01:42:09.580 --> 01:42:12.070
and within a couple of
months, we'll be seeing all 26

01:42:12.070 --> 01:42:15.250
of those projects finished
and all the awesome results

01:42:15.250 --> 01:42:17.292
from around the world.

01:42:17.292 --> 01:42:19.500
I want to just introduce
you to the team, in addition

01:42:19.500 --> 01:42:21.190
to myself.

01:42:21.190 --> 01:42:24.530
Derek and Bob and Shiaqi.

01:42:24.530 --> 01:42:27.340
It's all four of us
volunteering our time,

01:42:27.340 --> 01:42:32.430
this is a passion project for
us on the evening and weekends.

01:42:32.430 --> 01:42:35.040
What drew us to
Teach to Learn was

01:42:35.040 --> 01:42:37.530
all of our background
in music education,

01:42:37.530 --> 01:42:39.720
and musicians
ourselves, the countries

01:42:39.720 --> 01:42:41.370
we've worked in
around the world,

01:42:41.370 --> 01:42:44.130
and all that experience meeting
and interacting with people

01:42:44.130 --> 01:42:45.400
all around the world.

01:42:45.400 --> 01:42:47.070
So it's a very
international team

01:42:47.070 --> 01:42:49.490
and with a very
international focus.

01:42:53.180 --> 01:42:55.460
For the 15K Competition,
just to give you

01:42:55.460 --> 01:42:58.700
a little sense of how
that funding helped

01:42:58.700 --> 01:43:02.900
us advance the organization.

01:43:02.900 --> 01:43:06.140
A good chunk of that funding
went towards programming.

01:43:06.140 --> 01:43:10.100
A big part of that was
towards the Fellowship proof

01:43:10.100 --> 01:43:10.750
of concept.

01:43:10.750 --> 01:43:14.317
So we had this idea, as a
bit of an ambitious idea

01:43:14.317 --> 01:43:16.400
to do the Fellowship Program
when we didn't really

01:43:16.400 --> 01:43:19.355
have the funds to
make it happen,

01:43:19.355 --> 01:43:21.230
because we were funding
each of those Fellows

01:43:21.230 --> 01:43:22.850
to do those community projects.

01:43:22.850 --> 01:43:24.950
But it was a bit of
a chicken and egg

01:43:24.950 --> 01:43:28.910
because we wanted
to get universities,

01:43:28.910 --> 01:43:34.640
and maybe orchestras, and
other music programs involved

01:43:34.640 --> 01:43:37.430
and sponsoring Fellows,
but we didn't really

01:43:37.430 --> 01:43:40.910
have any kind of proof to
show what that program could

01:43:40.910 --> 01:43:43.680
look like, what those results
would actually look like.

01:43:43.680 --> 01:43:47.150
So the $15K could not have
come at a better time for us

01:43:47.150 --> 01:43:53.240
to short circuit that cycle and
skip ahead to actually having

01:43:53.240 --> 01:43:55.590
a proof of concept
now after 10 months,

01:43:55.590 --> 01:43:58.850
that we can take to
build partnerships

01:43:58.850 --> 01:44:01.490
with some of the partners
I mentioned and really

01:44:01.490 --> 01:44:04.917
have tangible evidence
of the impact.

01:44:04.917 --> 01:44:06.500
So in addition to
the proof of concept

01:44:06.500 --> 01:44:09.710
for that flagship
program, it's also

01:44:09.710 --> 01:44:12.440
helped us expand and
test different models

01:44:12.440 --> 01:44:13.400
for Classroom Connect.

01:44:13.400 --> 01:44:15.770
So that additional funding
has gone a long way

01:44:15.770 --> 01:44:19.460
in growing that part
of the business.

01:44:19.460 --> 01:44:24.530
And like I mentioned
earlier, we kind of

01:44:24.530 --> 01:44:27.380
doubled down in that area
after some of our conversations

01:44:27.380 --> 01:44:29.930
with our 15K mentor.

01:44:29.930 --> 01:44:31.490
Thinking about, OK,
I guess if people

01:44:31.490 --> 01:44:33.290
are willing to pay
for this service,

01:44:33.290 --> 01:44:35.540
this is an area we should
really investigate and try

01:44:35.540 --> 01:44:41.000
to perfect so that we can
support our hybrid business

01:44:41.000 --> 01:44:45.020
model of both revenue
and individual donations

01:44:45.020 --> 01:44:46.670
and grant funding.

01:44:46.670 --> 01:44:50.300
So that was really good
advice and we ran with it.

01:44:50.300 --> 01:44:52.880
On the other side,
we also put money

01:44:52.880 --> 01:44:57.380
towards editing, and
developing, and producing

01:44:57.380 --> 01:45:01.220
all of the really awesome
material that's been coming in.

01:45:01.220 --> 01:45:04.460
Derek and Bob over the
last summer were traveling,

01:45:04.460 --> 01:45:06.590
and I got to visit some
of our Fellows in person

01:45:06.590 --> 01:45:08.810
and capture some of the
work that they're doing.

01:45:11.690 --> 01:45:14.120
As well as the projects
are starting to ramp up,

01:45:14.120 --> 01:45:18.530
and Fellows are documenting
their activities.

01:45:18.530 --> 01:45:21.440
We just have a lot of really
interesting stuff coming in

01:45:21.440 --> 01:45:24.410
that we want to turn
into compelling materials

01:45:24.410 --> 01:45:28.070
and messaging that can help
us then bring these programs

01:45:28.070 --> 01:45:30.805
or any of these programs
to the new partners.

01:45:30.805 --> 01:45:32.180
And finally, we've
been investing

01:45:32.180 --> 01:45:35.360
in building our own
platform online.

01:45:35.360 --> 01:45:38.630
Right now, we're using readily
available, free-to-use tools

01:45:38.630 --> 01:45:40.890
for the most part to
run these programs.

01:45:40.890 --> 01:45:43.140
But our vision is to
have a place where

01:45:43.140 --> 01:45:46.220
our Fellows and other
participants can come log in

01:45:46.220 --> 01:45:49.490
and we can have more
control over the user

01:45:49.490 --> 01:45:50.780
experience in the future.

01:45:50.780 --> 01:45:54.980
But we're not quite there yet,
but we're to get there soon.

