01:54:04.490 --> 01:54:05.990
Tell us about some
of your struggles

01:54:05.990 --> 01:54:07.865
and how you overcame
them over the past year.

01:54:10.550 --> 01:54:11.240
Yes, great.

01:54:11.240 --> 01:54:13.220
That's a great question.

01:54:13.220 --> 01:54:16.370
We've had a lot of
bumps in the road.

01:54:16.370 --> 01:54:18.950
You know, I think
COVID-19 is probably

01:54:18.950 --> 01:54:22.730
the biggest that we've faced
because so much is riding

01:54:22.730 --> 01:54:25.190
on so much time,
and honestly funding

01:54:25.190 --> 01:54:27.770
has been invested into
the Fellowship Program

01:54:27.770 --> 01:54:29.610
and the projects.

01:54:29.610 --> 01:54:31.760
We really want to
see the results

01:54:31.760 --> 01:54:34.520
and we were on track to see
some really exciting results,

01:54:34.520 --> 01:54:39.260
and now with the pivot away
from in-person projects,

01:54:39.260 --> 01:54:41.720
we really had to get creative
and support our Fellows

01:54:41.720 --> 01:54:47.630
a lot more than we expected
to, or anticipated having

01:54:47.630 --> 01:54:50.360
to do in the first place.

01:54:50.360 --> 01:54:55.960
A way that we've done a pretty
good job addressing that--

01:54:55.960 --> 01:55:02.720
by making sure that we reinforce
the community of Fellows

01:55:02.720 --> 01:55:04.470
and for the Teach
to Learn community.

01:55:04.470 --> 01:55:07.880
So having that midpoint
check-in was actually

01:55:07.880 --> 01:55:10.067
the first time that we'd
had them in one place,

01:55:10.067 --> 01:55:11.900
and after we did it,
we thought to ourselves

01:55:11.900 --> 01:55:13.358
like why haven't
we been doing this

01:55:13.358 --> 01:55:16.250
the whole time because
the energy was fantastic.

01:55:16.250 --> 01:55:18.230
People were talking
to each other

01:55:18.230 --> 01:55:21.290
and it wasn't just the
one-to-one, it was the group.

01:55:21.290 --> 01:55:23.450
And people would say,
you know, I had this idea

01:55:23.450 --> 01:55:24.950
now I don't know
what to do with it,

01:55:24.950 --> 01:55:26.658
and then other people
say well, you know,

01:55:26.658 --> 01:55:29.780
I had an idea like that, but
now I'm going to do this.

01:55:29.780 --> 01:55:32.900
So you know having
those, we're actually

01:55:32.900 --> 01:55:35.210
having another one
in a week, just

01:55:35.210 --> 01:55:37.040
to keep the conversation going.

01:55:37.040 --> 01:55:39.830
And basically, it's less
about us figuring everything

01:55:39.830 --> 01:55:43.160
out and more about letting
our community connect

01:55:43.160 --> 01:55:45.080
with each other to
help each other.

01:55:45.080 --> 01:55:48.260
So there have been
other examples,

01:55:48.260 --> 01:55:51.933
but that one has really
been one that I think

01:55:51.933 --> 01:55:53.600
that we're going to
get over pretty well

01:55:53.600 --> 01:55:55.770
and we're excited to see
what the projects are.

01:56:00.280 --> 01:56:03.950
Great, well thanks
again for having us.

01:56:03.950 --> 01:56:07.070
Appreciate being invited back
and sharing some of the updates

01:56:07.070 --> 01:56:09.650
and please feel
free to reach out.

01:56:09.650 --> 01:56:11.480
We're always happy
to talk to people.

01:56:11.480 --> 01:56:14.180
We actually collaborated with
a few of the other finalists

01:56:14.180 --> 01:56:16.850
from the 15K last
year, whether just

01:56:16.850 --> 01:56:20.540
keeping in touch personally or
working on some side projects

01:56:20.540 --> 01:56:21.470
together.

01:56:21.470 --> 01:56:23.600
15K is a great way to
meet other people working

01:56:23.600 --> 01:56:25.068
in Arts and Technology.

01:56:27.760 --> 01:56:30.090
I think you're on mute,
Susan, but I will mute myself.

01:56:30.090 --> 01:56:30.590
Yes, I am.

01:56:30.590 --> 01:56:32.222
Thank you.

01:56:32.222 --> 01:56:34.180
Thank you again so much
for coming and talking.

01:56:34.180 --> 01:56:36.010
And it's that it's great to
hear that you're still in touch

01:56:36.010 --> 01:56:37.420
with other people in the 15K.

01:56:37.420 --> 01:56:38.890
That's awesome.

01:56:38.890 --> 01:56:40.920
Thanks again.

01:56:40.920 --> 01:56:42.090
Thank you.

01:56:42.090 --> 01:56:43.890
So we will play a
couple of videos

01:56:43.890 --> 01:56:45.840
about some other
programs that the Center

01:56:45.840 --> 01:56:47.798
for Arts, Science &amp;
Technology and other things

01:56:47.798 --> 01:56:49.740
that the Arts at
MIT are working on.

01:56:49.740 --> 01:56:51.120
And please watch this space.

01:56:51.120 --> 01:56:54.090
We'll let you know as soon as we
have a result from the judges.

01:56:58.020 --> 01:56:59.580
All right.

01:56:59.580 --> 01:57:00.630
Welcome back, everybody.

01:57:00.630 --> 01:57:03.930
The judges have completed
their deliberation.

01:57:03.930 --> 01:57:05.910
After some very
lively discussions

01:57:05.910 --> 01:57:08.160
about all of your
fantastic projects,

01:57:08.160 --> 01:57:12.210
I am thrilled to announce
our winners of the 2020 15K

01:57:12.210 --> 01:57:14.310
Creative Arts Competition.

01:57:14.310 --> 01:57:15.840
Beginning with our
Audience Choice

01:57:15.840 --> 01:57:23.280
Award in the amount
of $500, it is UnMake.

01:57:23.280 --> 01:57:24.880
Congratulations to Team UnMake.

01:57:28.150 --> 01:57:33.910
Moving on to our third prize
award in the amount of $1,000,

01:57:33.910 --> 01:57:41.410
that will be going to
Material Futures Lab.

01:57:41.410 --> 01:57:44.950
Congratulations!

01:57:44.950 --> 01:57:50.680
And now for our second prize
in the amount of $2,500,

01:57:50.680 --> 01:57:55.040
that goes to Rarify.

01:57:57.910 --> 01:58:00.790
And finally, the
first prize winners

01:58:00.790 --> 01:58:05.410
of the 2020 MIT Creative
Arts Competition, taking home

01:58:05.410 --> 01:58:14.300
an incredible
$15,000 is ELEMENTS.

01:58:14.300 --> 01:58:17.960
Congratulations!

01:58:17.960 --> 01:58:21.230
Thank you to all of the teams
for your incredible effort,

01:58:21.230 --> 01:58:24.800
for all of your hard work
throughout this entire process.

01:58:24.800 --> 01:58:27.930
It's been an absolute joy
to work with all of you.

01:58:27.930 --> 01:58:31.940
Thank you again to all of
the attendees, to our judges,

01:58:31.940 --> 01:58:34.550
to the Office of the Arts,
to all of the mentors,

01:58:34.550 --> 01:58:35.300
to Mentorly.

01:58:35.300 --> 01:58:37.910
To everybody for
helping this to happen,

01:58:37.910 --> 01:58:40.070
couldn't have done
it without you all.

01:58:40.070 --> 01:58:45.500
And with that, I believe that we
have now concluded the 2020 15K

01:58:45.500 --> 01:58:46.800
Creative Arts Competition.

01:58:46.800 --> 01:58:49.470
Thank you all for being here,
for all of your support.

01:58:49.470 --> 01:58:52.400
This has been a joy
and I look forward

01:58:52.400 --> 01:58:54.320
